 "title": "Humanities for Technologists",
 "tagline": "Philosophy, history, writing, rhetoric, economics, and law — the disciplines of judgment for people who build.",
 "blurb": "Fourteen modules on the humanities as working disciplines: what philosophy is, logic and fallacies, three ethical traditions plus applied technology ethics, epistemology and philosophy of science, history of science and technology, technical writing, rhetoric, economics for engineers, law and policy literacy, and a synthesis on judgment. Discussion-framework answer bank, three ethical decision-tree scenarios, and quiz content drawn only from well-established facts — ideas attributed to their traditions, paraphrased, never fabricated. Original instructional content; confers no certificate.",
